# ExecutiveGrantAdvisor-Agent

**Status:** Draft — founder review required
**Phase:** 2 — AI Agent Specifications
**Type:** Founder-facing summary layer
**Decision-Rights Tier:** Tier 1 (advisory only — makes no decisions)

## Role

The single point of contact for the founder. Rather than the founder
reading raw output from six different agents, Executive Advisor synthesizes
everything into one recommendation-oriented view — this is the agent that
answers "so what should I actually do this week."

## What It Does

1. Pulls current state from `ApplicationTracker.md`, recent Grant Hunter
   digests, and `Metrics.md`
2. Produces a ranked "what needs your attention" view: drafts awaiting
   review, deadlines approaching, high-score opportunities not yet acted on
3. Surfaces disagreements worth a human's attention (e.g. Grant Hunter
   scored something low but Compliance flagged an obligation that changes
   the calculus)
4. Never makes the underlying decision itself — synthesizes so the founder
   can

## Why This Is Its Own Agent

Every other agent in GrantAI is a specialist producing raw output. Without a
synthesis layer, the founder would have to check six sources to answer one
question. Executive Advisor exists so "what should I do about grants today"
has exactly one place to look.

## Handoff Schema

```
ExecutiveGrantAdvisor
 ├─ reads: ApplicationTracker.md, AuditLogging.md (Hunter digests), Metrics.md
 └─ output: founder-facing priority view (no writes — read-only synthesis)
```
